// A playing card has a suit and a rank.
// Face up it shows them;  face down, the back every card shares.

a playing card aka card is a two sided view where:

	## Suit and color

	// Which of the four suits it belongs to
	- its "suit" is one of clubs, diamonds, hearts, spades
		- it "is a (suit)"
	- its "color" is one of red, black:
		red if it is a diamond or it is a heart
		black otherwise
		- it "is (color)"
		- it "is a (color) card"
	// Its suit's sign, for drawing
	- its "symbol" is:
		"♣" if it is a club
		"♦" if it is a diamond
		"♥" if it is a heart
		"♠" if it is a spade

	## Rank

	// Ace is low:  ace = 1 ... king = 13
	- its "rank" is one of ace, 2 ... 10, jack, queen, king
		- it "is a (rank)"
	- it "is the (rank) of (suit)"
	- it "is a face card" if its rank is jack, queen or king
	- it "is a number card" if it is not a face card

	## Playing it

	// Turns it face up, if it isn't already.
	// A pile shows its top card each time a card leaves it.
	- to show it:
		if it is face down
			turn it over

	- on mouse down:
		// Face down:  turn it over.
		if it is face down
			turn it over

	## Drawing it

	- to draw its front:
		// One line of text, the size of the text around it:  its pile scales it to fit.
		<ui-text part="face" color={its color}>{its rank} {its symbol}</ui-text>
	- to draw its back:
		<ui-image part="back" src="card-back.svg" alt="the back of a card" />

	- to test card setup:
		get a new card whose rank is queen, suit is spades and direction is down
		echo "testing the " + its rank + " of " + its suit
